1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,580
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,520
Before Le Tianyi died, he said

3
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,000
that he didn't kill Wen.

4
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,280
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

5
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,080
He was lying.

6
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,360
I saw it with my own eyes.

7
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,080
Why didn't you call the cops back then?

8
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:37,560
I was scared.

9
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,720
I was afraid they'd leak the videos.

10
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,840
Then I'd be completely ruined.

11
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,400
Don't be scared.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,040
Mom's here.

13
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:01,880
As long as I'm around...

14
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,240
nobody gets away.

15
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,080
(Jin Keke saw Le Tianyi kill Wen)

16
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:10,840
(with her own eyes.)

17
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,360
(But what if Le Tianyi wasn't lying?)

18
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,960
(What if the real killer
is still alive?)

19
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,240
(Then what did you actually see?)

20
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,680
(Is it a memory you made up)

21
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:23,160
(to keep yourself going?)

22
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:27,880
(Or were you lying all along?)

23
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:32,460
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 26=

24
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,200
The drone footage the police have

25
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,760
was deliberately left behind
by Ms. Song.

26
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,440
She must have started

27
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:49,960
suspecting you back then.

28
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,440
We found out Song Yalan worked
as an engineer

29
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,120
at Longfan Shengxing Chemical Plant

30
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,640
for five years
before she became a teacher.

31
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,960
Mainly responsible
for chemical formulation.

32
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:00,280
(Her resignation file says
she left the company)

33
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,240
(to switch to education.)

34
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:02,560
(Her suitcase)

35
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,200
(is full of books
on explosive principles)

36
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,040
(and mechanical manufacturing.)

37
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,680
We searched the abandoned water tower

38
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,080
and found blueprints
for rocket launchers

39
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,520
and homemade guns
designed by Song Yalan.

40
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,120
She poured hours

41
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,720
into grinding through all this stuff,

42
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,200
hand you these tools

43
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,280
for revenge.

44
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,680
Put it on.

45
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,960
Then you, Wen, and I

46
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,800
will truly be connected.

47
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,840
Wen can feel

48
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,560
your heartbeat.

49
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:53,440
I can feel your determination.

50
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,880
If one day

51
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,640
you waver or get scared,

52
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,120
just touch it.

53
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:05,160
Think about how Wen looked
when she died.

54
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,560
Think about how good Wen was to you.

55
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:38,320
She finally had a home

56
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,840
and a mom.

57
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,160
Even if that mom was stolen,

58
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,560
she refused to let go

59
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:48,240
of that gentle rope.

60
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:29,940
(Middle School)

61
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,680
(Jin Keke!)

62
00:06:38,850 --> 00:06:43,180
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

63
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,200
(Qin Ming!)

64
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:46,840
(Qin Ming!)

65
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,320
(Qin Ming!)

66
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:56,360
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

67
00:07:05,290 --> 00:07:09,210
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

68
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,960
Leave the soda before you go.

69
00:07:12,690 --> 00:07:16,330
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

70
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:19,720
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

71
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:22,440
You seem to like coming to the rooftop.

72
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,400
You're following me?

73
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,000
No.

74
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,040
I just

75
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,680
happen to like rooftops too.

76
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,440
Why?

77
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,160
If you think of the human eye
as a camera,

78
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:42,520
when we read books,
look at test papers or the blackboard,

79
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,920
everything in our eyes
is a medium close-up or a close-up.

80
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,480
The field of view is narrow.

81
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,640
But once you get to the rooftop,

82
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,760
the view suddenly opens up.

83
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,080
The eye's wide-angle mode turns on,

84
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,480
and the world suddenly feels bigger.

85
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:06,440
Sounds like a camera manual.

86
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,960
But I get it.

87
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,800
Standing here,

88
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:15,160
you feel the sun
is close enough to touch.

89
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,800
But it's 150 million kilometers away
from us.

90
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,280
All we see every day

91
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:24,160
is just a beam of light
that took eight minutes to get here.

92
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,160
Most of what people believe in

93
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:29,440
their whole lives
is this kind of illusion.

94
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,600
You think it's close enough,

95
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,800
but it's actually far away.

96
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,480
Hey, what are you doing?

97
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,080
We...

98
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,240
What class are you in?

99
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,320
What's your name?

100
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,240
Can't you see that huge seal?

101
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,520
No going up to the rooftop!
Get down here!

102
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:12,020
(Class 2, Senior 3)

103
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:17,180
(Class 2, Senior 3)

104
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:20,700
(Class 2, Senior 3)

105
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,360
(In an ethylene molecule,
the carbon and hydrogen atoms)

106
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,360
(all lie in the same plane.)

107
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,760
(If each double-bonded carbon atom)

108
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,960
(in an ethylene molecule)

109
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,320
(is connected to two different atoms)

110
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,520
(or atomic groups...)

111
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:41,840
(Qin Ming.)

112
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,560
Qin Ming.

113
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,160
You're late again.

114
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,160
(Location)

115
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:52,960
Qin Ming,

116
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,040
the fact that you're standing here

117
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:57,000
means you actually went
through the homework

118
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,280
I left you.

119
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,040
Ms. Song.

120
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,400
It's time to end this.

121
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:09,160
No. It's time for class.

122
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,880
(The Last Lesson)
Sit down.

123
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,720
Song Yalan's location is locked.

124
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,560
Let's go!

125
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,200
Got it!

126
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,560
One of a teacher's duties

127
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,480
is to answer her students' questions.

128
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,920
Go ahead and ask.

129
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,360
Your answer

130
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,560
for Le Tianyi's death
wasn't the right one.

131
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,280
Impressive.

132
00:10:58,720 --> 00:10:59,920
As expected of you, Qin Ming.

133
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,920
So what's your answer?

134
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:05,080
You couldn't have turned Le Tianyi

135
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,800
into pig feed all by yourself.

136
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,840
But both Jin Keke and Wang Xuan

137
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,520
had alibis that day.

138
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,640
Then who do you think it was?

139
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:14,880
I think

140
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,320
that person is already dead.

141
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:40,560
Who are you?

142
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,160
I didn't kill her.

143
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,400
Really, it wasn't me.

144
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,040
Mr. Zhang.

145
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,840
Zhang Xiaodong!

146
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,240
It's him!

147
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,440
He told me to kill your daughter!

148
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,120
You killed my daughter!

149
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:13,800
Uncle Le.

150
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,640
Tianyi,

151
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,760
she doesn't seem dead yet.
Still breathing.

152
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:37,760
Uncle Le.

153
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,200
She's dead.

154
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:41,560
Uncle Le.

155
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,560
She's dead.

156
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,080
I said she's dead. Did you hear me?

157
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:45,960
Uncle Le.

158
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:46,880
Yeah, she's dead.

159
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,720
Dead.

160
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,200
Dead.

161
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,240
Bury.

162
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,440
Hurry up!

163
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,400
Move faster!

164
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:05,680
Forgot to tell you.

165
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,960
Zhang Xiaoya was buried alive
by Le Tianyi.

166
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,280
Mr. Zhang.

167
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,600
Mr. Zhang?

168
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:43,880
Xiaoya,

169
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,120
I've avenged you.

170
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:10,680
Go ahead and ask.

171
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,480
Who

172
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,520
killed Zhang Xiaodong?

173
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,160
Didn't Zhang Xiaodong tell you?

174
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,560
Dr. Qin,

175
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:38,800
isn't it said that corpses talk?

176
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,360
Our autopsy results show

177
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,280
Zhang Xiaodong drowned.

178
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,360
Drowned? So he killed himself!

179
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,040
Ms. Song.

180
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,440
That's just playing with words.

181
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:57,080
Isn't playing games exactly
what you love, Zhang Xiaodong?

182
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:58,800
I'll stab you all I want!

183
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:04,560
Why won't you leave her alone?

184
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,640
Why couldn't you just let her go?

185
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,520
She was only seventeen.

186
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,720
Why did you...?

187
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,000
Mr. Zhang,

188
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:22,560
you like watching your prey struggle,
don't you?

189
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:24,880
I'm gonna kill you.

190
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,320
I'll kill you!

191
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:55,000
The water's full of your pets.

192
00:15:56,400 --> 00:16:00,200
They love the blood of animals.

193
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,000
But he forgot

194
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:16,640
that collectibles can resent the master

195
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,800
who stares at them.

196
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:22,840
Now, it's his turn
to be the prey on display.

197
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:26,320
In that cold, dark swamp,

198
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:29,440
his prized cold-bloodedness and greed

199
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,240
look so pathetic and weak

200
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,880
in front of

201
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,000
his true kind.

202
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:37,600
Qin Ming,

203
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:40,160
the more you struggle,
the more this poison hurts.

204
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:40,960
If you want to live,

205
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,280
finish the last lesson
like a good student.

206
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:47,240
Listen.

207
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,720
The sound of bones being torn apart

208
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:54,920
(The Last Lesson)
is his finest tribute as a collectible!

209
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,040
Have you ever thought

210
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,600
about how you're any different
from those scumbags

211
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,400
like Zhang Xiaodong?

212
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:01,920
You destroyed yourself,

213
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:03,640
and you destroyed Jin Keke.

214
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,240
She saw you as a mother,

215
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,800
but you turned killing people
into her way of repaying you,

216
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:10,000
making her commit monstrous crimes!

217
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,800
You're more terrifying
than that demon Zhang Xiaodong.

218
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:15,320
He only wanted to destroy
people's bodies.

219
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,440
But you destroy people's souls.

220
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,120
Now it's my turn to ask you.

221
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,320
Do you know

222
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:28,880
why you're the one here today
for the last lesson?

223
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,200
(Keke!)

224
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,200
At first, I thought

225
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,400
she just wanted to run a test

226
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,680
to see how much you valued her.

227
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,160
But later I realized

228
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:56,040
she wanted to tell us a truth

229
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,680
before her death.

230
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,000
You

231
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,280
saved her.

232
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,800
I

233
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,640
was going to forgive her.

234
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,560
But now I can't.

235
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:12,920
Ms. Song,

236
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:16,000
you had the lawyer pass
a message to her,

237
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,320
didn't you?

238
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:20,520
She's completely broken down.

239
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,960
She used to see you

240
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,960
as her last emotional anchor.

241
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,200
(Mom, I miss you. I miss you.)

242
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,720
Why did you have to be so cruel?

243
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:28,760
Cruel?

244
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:31,920
Qin Ming,

245
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:33,440
you're calling me cruel?

246
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:34,880
Fine.

247
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,040
Let me tell you why!

248
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,160
I wanted her to feel

249
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,760
the most extreme despair!

250
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:46,080
Not fear. Not pain.

251
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:48,480
(The Last Lesson)
It's that despair

252
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,720
(The Last Lesson)
of being pushed off a cliff!

253
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,600
Just like what Wen went through!

254
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,240
(Qin.)

255
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,800
(Jin Keke just killed herself
at the hospital.)

256
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:32,690
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

257
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:37,230
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

258
00:19:37,450 --> 00:19:41,500
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

259
00:19:41,950 --> 00:19:46,060
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

260
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:58,690
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

261
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:01,590
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

262
00:20:02,190 --> 00:20:05,810
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

263
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:10,030
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

264
00:20:10,030 --> 00:20:14,780
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

265
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:19,060
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

266
00:20:19,810 --> 00:20:23,580
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

267
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:27,930
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

268
00:20:36,630 --> 00:20:40,830
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

269
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:45,160
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

270
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:48,960
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

271
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:51,830
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

272
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:56,650
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

273
00:20:56,650 --> 00:21:01,270
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

274
00:21:01,270 --> 00:21:03,600
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

275
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,670
♪We stop here in this night♪

276
00:21:05,670 --> 00:21:10,100
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

277
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:16,010
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

278
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:24,800
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

279
00:21:36,370 --> 00:21:43,320
